<tr>
    <td  bgcolor="#c0c0c0" valign="TOP"><table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" border="0">
<tr>
    <td  bgcolor="#c0c0c0" width="100%" valign="top"><tt><font color="#000000">
Author:&nbsp;<a href="/showmember.php?name=Espirius">Espirius</a>&nbsp;(---.001.popsite.net)<br>
Date:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;08-05-01 21:14<br>
<br><HTML>This is the letter I sent to EQ customer service tonite. Please read and comment.<br>
<br>
E<br>
----------------------------------------------<br>
<br>
<br>
Good evening and thank you for your time.<br>
 <br>
I would like to open by saying thank you for your development staff and to the many people at Sony and Verant whom have spent<br>
many sleepless nights making Norrath and enjoyable place.<br>
 <br>
At least up until now. <br>
 <br>
Let me first explain the situation. <br>
 <br>
I was sitting in the zone Qeynos Hills camping and NPC by the name of Hadden (who drops an item called the Fishbone Earring)<br>
I had been there for roughly three hours, by myself, waiting patiently for him to appear. About 2 or 3 pm this afternoon I see a man<br>
sit on the hill behind me, as that he doesn't say anything I let him be (many people wait to take their turn at this camp spot). Well now<br>
keep in mind this is roughly a six hour spawn (as I'm told, this is longest I've ever waited) and I've been sitting there patiently the whole<br>
time waiting for the NPC to appear. In case the person reading this doesn't play much.. the area is also compromised of 3 more NPCs<br>
One necromancer, a warrior, and a mage of some sort on the opposite side of the lake, all of which aggro when you attack Hadden.<br>
Hadden spawns finally, so with my Harmony spell ready, I cast it on all three other NPCs (so they don't all attack me at once and <br>
kill me). Well while I'm doing this the man sitting on the hill is already on Hadden, being a 50 druid he makes rather short work of <br>
him. (I am a 30 ranger) I walk up to him and I say "Excuse me? I believe I was here first?" He turns to me and says "So?"<br>
I explain to him that I have been sitting there for roughly three hours, and he saw me sitting there when he logged in and <br>
appeared. He said "Yes, I logged and came back". I then informed him that once you leave a zone being that logging off or zoning,<br>
the area is considered 'uncamped' and someone else can take over. He said something to the effect that he was there first - this morning.<br>
.. and before I could say anything else he ported himself away.<br>
 <br>
Now I didn't get a report, but I took screenshots of the conversation, which will be attached to this email for your study - I wanted <br>
hardcopies for myself, so this is the way to do it.<br>
 <br>
I petitioned for intervention to the situation, because I was obviously wronged.... it does not seem right that a character 20 levels above me<br>
can simply walk into my camp, do as he likes, and leave because he can...<br>
 <br>
I first spoke to Guide Cait. I explained the situation to him/her and they told me they could not do anything, and would forward it to a GM for<br>
further consideration.  A few hours later I spoke to GM Phyllum. I explained the situation to him, and he proceeded to inform me that because<br>
I did not hit Hadden first, that the character known as Ralder was not Kill Stealing. However, I informed him again that I couldn't because I <br>
had to play defensively first (see above). He again said there was nothing he could do. <br>
 <br>
What I am seeking is a resolution to this issue in-game. I feel cheated of my time (3 hours) and my integrity ( I was earning my keep)<br>
.I understand there are rules you abide to as well, so I am seeking a middle ground on this issue. I have been playing Everquest for nearly<br>
 a year now, I have brought in 6 other <br>
regular players and play regularly myself. I run my own business in real life www.nextco.com - an Internet provider... as well as being a loan<br>
officer in my spare time during the workweek - I only mention these things to set that I too am a business man and would again appreciate <br>
being able to come to a co-operative decision on this.<br>
 <br>
What I am seeking is ONE of these things<br>
a) I am reimbursed in game for my effort - The Fishbone Earring itself or half of its market value  - 1000 platinum pieces<br>
b) suspension (of at least 4 days) or punishment of some sort for the account holder of Ralder - with documentation from the customer service dept stating <br>
     what was done and for how long. <br>
 <br>
In either case, I would like my letter to be pooled with those that is read when reviewing the effectiveness of your 'Play Nice Policy', as <br>
that this character did not 'play nice'. <br>
 <br>
If we cannot come to a resolution, I am afraid that I would be considering canceling my account. Of the three or four times in a year and a half<br>
I've needed to contact a GM I always seem to get the same answer "We can't do that, we must keep things uniform", which unfortunately to <br>
me means 'We have to let the 'bad guys' get away with everything otherwise everyone would complain' -which is understandable. I just wish<br>
that the GMs could take on more accountability for those who choose to 'bend the rules' or push the 'Play Nice Policy' to it's limit. <br>
 <br>
I thank your for your courteous and prompt response to my letter, it is my sincere wish that we can have a fair and equitable solution that<br>
fits both our needs. I enjoy being part of EverQuest. I would hate to have something petty take away from all that, and this would also restore my<br>
faith in the Guide Program that Verant has created.<br>
 <br>
 <br>
 <br>
Sincerely<br>
 <br>
 <br>
Chris McMahel<br>
NextCo Internet Services<br>
Executive Sales and Consulting<br>
 <br>
 <br>
 <br>
Cazic-Thule Server<br>
Character : Espirius</HTML></font></tt><p>
